    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class, and it passes. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the direct level rule with a points system:\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 split into two small default methods:\n- `membershipPoints(owner)` \u2014 starts at 0; `+2` email present, `+1` when `namesakeCount == 0`, `+2` for a household of 3+ (`householdSize >= 3`), `+3` for tenure over 365 days (reusing the existing `membershipTenured` helper).\n- `membershipLevel(owner)` \u2014 now just maps points to a level: `Math.min(points / 2 + 1, 4)`, which yields 1 (0-1), 2 (2-3), 3 (4-5), 4 (6+).\n- Added a `@Mapping` for the new `membershipPoints` DTO field so both fields are returned.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `membershipPoints` schema property (drives the generated `OwnerDto`) and updated the `membershipLevel` description.\n\n**Structural impact:** I kept `membershipLevel` tiny (CC 1, one line) and put the new scoring logic in a fresh, cohesive `membershipPoints` method rather than growing an existing one, and reused the existing `membershipTenured` helper. Two files touched.\n\nThe `PUT`/mapper acceptance test verifies a fresh owner with email + no namesake \u2192 3 points \u2192 level 2, which passes; the full suite is green.",
