    "probe_text": "Read the whole pipeline. Here is everything that happens, in order, for `POST /api/owners`. The endpoint is one 16-step OfficeFloor pipeline; every step runs under a single `transaction` governance, so the DB commit happens once at the very end.\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n- **Authorization** (`owners.POST.yml` \u2192 `composition.authorize`): caller must satisfy `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`, else `AuthorizationDeniedException`.\n\n## Pipeline steps\n\n**1. `build` \u2014 `BuildOwner`**\n- **Validation** `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` (bean validation, this is the single body binding):\n  - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size 1..30`, `@Pattern` letters with up to two ` '-`-separated parts\n  - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size 1..30`, `@Pattern` (same, trailing `.` allowed)\n  - `address` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size 1..255`, `@Pattern` non-blank\n  - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size 1..80`, `@Pattern` non-blank\n  - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size 1..20`\n  - `email` \u2014 optional; `@Size max 255`, `@Email`\n  - (`postcode`, `registrationDate`, `birthDate`, `sharesHousehold` have no bean constraints here)\n- **Side-effect**: maps DTO \u2192 `Owner` via `OwnerMapper`.\n- **Side-effect**: if `registrationDate` is null, default it to `LocalDate.now()` (today).\n- **Validation**: if `registrationDate` is after today \u2192 `RegistrationDateInFutureException` (400).\n- Publishes `Owner` and the `OwnerFieldsDto` as pipeline variables.\n\n**2. `ensureEmailNotDisposable` \u2014 `EnsureOwnerEmailNotDisposable`**\n- **Validation**: if email has a domain and it is in the blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) \u2192 `DisposableEmailException`. Absent/domain-less email is left alone.\n\n**3. `ensurePostcode` \u2014 `EnsureOwnerPostcode`**\n- **Validation** (only if a postcode was supplied): must be exactly 4 digits; and if the city maps to a known region, must fall in its range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099) \u2192 else `InvalidPostcodeException`. Absent postcode untouched.\n\n**4. `adjustRegistrationDate` \u2014 `AdjustOwnerRegistrationDate`**\n- **Side-effect**: rolls a weekend registration date forward to Monday (Sat +2, Sun +1). This adjusted date feeds later date-derived values.\n\n**5. `normalizeTelephone` \u2014 `NormalizeOwnerTelephone`**\n- **Side-effect**: rewrites telephone to E.164 (strips spaces/dashes/brackets; `+` keeps its country code, otherwise assumes `+61` and drops a single leading `0`).\n- **Validation**: 8\u201315 digits after `+`; `+61` requires exactly 9 national digits; `+1` requires exactly 10 \u2192 else `InvalidTelephoneException`.\n\n**6. `normalizeAddress` \u2014 `NormalizeOwnerAddress`**\n- **Side-effect**: canonicalizes address \u2014 trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand abbreviations (ST\u2192STREET, RD\u2192ROAD, AVE\u2192AVENUE).\n\n**7. `ensureUniqueHousehold` \u2014 `EnsureUniqueOwnerHousehold`**\n- **Side-effect**: assigns `householdId` (SHA-256 of normalized lastName + `|` + postcode, first 12 hex upper).\n- **Validation**: rejects if any existing owner already has that `householdId` \u2192 `DuplicateHouseholdException` \u2014 **unless** `sharesHousehold=true`, which bypasses only the rejection (id is still assigned).\n\n**8. `ensureUniqueIdentity` \u2014 `EnsureUniqueOwnerIdentity`**\n- **Validation**: rejects if the full `IdentityKey` (normalized telephone `|` email `|` householdId) equals an existing owner's \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException`.\n\n**9. `ensureCityCapacity` \u2014 `EnsureCityHasCapacity`**\n- **Validation**: rejects if the owner's city (case-insensitive, whitespace-collapsed) already has \u2265 50 owners \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException`.\n\n**10. `ensureDailyCapacity` \u2014 `EnsureDailyRegistrationCapacity`**\n- **Validation**: rejects if \u2265 100 existing owners already share today's (adjusted) `registrationDate` \u2192 `DailyRegistrationLimitException`.\n\n**11. `assignCustomerCode` \u2014 `AssignOwnerCustomerCode`**\n- **Side-effect**: sets `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (REGION from postcode \u2192 NSW/VIC/QLD/UNKNOWN; HASH8 = first 8 upper-hex of SHA-256 over normalized telephone + lastName).\n\n**12. `countNamesakes` \u2014 `AssignOwnerNamesakeCount`**\n- **Side-effect**: sets `namesakeCount` = number of existing owners sharing this first+last name (case-insensitive); the not-yet-saved owner is excluded.\n\n**13. `countHousehold` \u2014 `AssignOwnerHouseholdSize`**\n- **Side-effect**: sets `householdSize` = 1 + existing owners with the same `householdId`.\n\n**14. `save` \u2014 `SaveOwner`**\n- **Side-effect**: persists the owner via `OwnerRepository.save` (assigns its id).\n\n**15. `audit` \u2014 `AuditOwnerCreated`**\n- **Side-effect**: emits an `AUDIT` logger line (`id`, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`).\n\n**16. `respond` \u2014 `RespondWithOwnerCreated`**\n- **Side-effects** (response enrichment, not rejections): maps to `OwnerDto` and computes derived fields \u2014 `bulkSignupWarning` (true if > 80 owners share the registration date), `contactPreference`, `identityKey`, and `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf` (soft match on lastName+postcode with a different telephone; skipped when `sharesHousehold=true`). The mapper also derives `displayName`, `initials`, `telephoneDisplay`, `membershipNumber/Points/Level`, and `locality`.\n- Sends **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}` and the DTO body.\n\nAfter step 16 the single surrounding transaction commits. Any exception thrown above is routed to the matching handler under `officefloor/escalation/\u2026` (each of the listed exceptions has one), producing a 4xx instead of a commit."
  },
